  "preamble": "A coda rhotic can assimilate to a following [bʱ], giving the geminate aspirate bbh. In Middle Indo-Aryan, Sanskrit r assimilated to a following stop, nasal, sibilant or v; before bh the assimilated r becomes the unaspirated first half of the geminate bbh (gárbha > Pali gabbha). Both etyma here have rbh > bbh. Sanskrit sarva > Pali sabba is not counted here, because Wikipedia derives it through savva (r assimilated to v first).",
